# ===========================================================================
# forgeloop — .gitignore
# This repo is intended to become open source. Be conservative: never commit
# secrets, credentials, or large trained-model weights.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Internal working docs (not part of the open-source release) ---
# `docs/` itself is the published Sphinx site and IS tracked; only the internal
# working notes inside it stay out.
docs/PLAN.md

# The docs notebook gallery is assembled from the books by
# scripts/build_forgeloop.py at docs-build time. The books are the source; a
# committed copy here would be a third duplicate of every chapter notebook.
docs/4-notebook-examples/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
*.egg
build/
dist/
*.whl
.eggs/

# --- Virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# --- Tooling caches ---
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- Jupyter ---
.ipynb_checkpoints/
# Executed notebooks are per-run artifacts — never check in.
*_executed.ipynb

# --- LaTeX build artifacts (in case any stray build output appears) ---
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz

# ===========================================================================
# Trained-model weights & large binaries — NOT committed (regenerate or fetch
# separately; see each topic's code/README). Keeps clones lean for OSS.
# Policy: exclude the heavy binaries by file type; keep the small JSON /
# metadata / README files that live alongside them in the store dirs.
# ===========================================================================
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.gguf
# HuggingFace tokenizer blobs are large and regenerated on model download.
**/tokenizer.json
**/vocab.json
**/merges.txt
**/spiece.model
**/*.spm

# ===========================================================================
# Generated artifacts — regenerate via each topic's scripts/, never commit.
# Policy: "outputs out, inputs in." Trained stores/adapters, backups, and
# script result/report files stay out; authored corpora, datasets, probes,
# eval cohorts, and config fixtures stay in.
# ===========================================================================
# Trained GMS stores & model/adapter output dirs
**/data/gms_*_store*/
**/data/gms_regulatory_cap*/
**/data/lab_stores/
**/data/stores/
**/data/*_classifier/
**/data/*_classifier_*/
**/data/*_lora/
**/data/draft_response_*/
**/data/extract_encoder_*/
# Backups / snapshots
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.pre_schema/
# Generated knowledge-graph visualizations
**/kg_*.html
# Generated result / report / diagnostic / log outputs
**/data/benchmark_*.json
**/data/doe_*.csv
**/data/capstone_*.csv
**/data/capstone_*.json
# ...except the pinned campaign results. These are outputs, but regenerating
# them needs a full DoE campaign against the licensed substrate, and ~11
# analysis notebooks across Ship-and-Pray and Prompt-and-Pray do nothing but
# read them. At ~50 KB of JSON they are cheap to carry, and carrying them is
# the difference between those notebooks working or failing for a reader with
# no knowlytix license. The trained stores stay out -- 00_setup.ipynb rebuilds
# those from committed corpora.
!**/data/capstone_run.json
!**/data/capstone_rows.json
!**/data/capstone_companions.json
!**/data/capstone_retrieval.json
# The pinned test set and the captured trajectory follow the same reasoning:
# capstone_run.py reads the test set and only re-materializes it when absent,
# so shipping it keeps the campaign reproducible rather than freshly sampled,
# and 09_agentic_capstone.ipynb reads the trajectory directly.
!**/data/capstone_testset.json
!**/data/capstone_trajectory_example.json
# Completes the seven-entry Ship-and-Pray set that artifacts.py declares, so
# missing_artifacts() can actually come back empty.
!**/data/capstone_newprops.json
**/data/*_calibration.json
**/data/*_results.json
**/*_augmented.jsonl
**/data/**/rag_doe_*.json
**/data/**/compare_parsers_results.json
**/data/corpus_facts.md
**/data/**/*.log.jsonl

# ===========================================================================
# Secrets & credentials — NEVER commit (defensive; open-source repo)
# ===========================================================================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.lic
*.p12
*.pfx
# The knowlytix licence lives in ~/.knowlytix/license.key; ignore any copy of
# that directory that lands in a checkout.
.knowlytix/
license.key
credentials.json
service-account-*.json
.aws/
.gcp/
.ssh/
id_rsa
id_rsa.pub
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.pub

# --- Claude Code working state ---
# Ignored wholesale, not file-by-file. A per-book `.claude/skills/` here once
# carried internal engineering notes -- private branch names, local checkout
# paths and a list of the substrate internals that must not be described in
# public -- and it shipped simply because nothing excluded it. Agent working
# notes are written for a private machine; this repo is world-readable. If a
# skill or hook is genuinely meant for readers, `git add -f` it deliberately.
.claude/
**/.claude/

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.vscode/
.idea/

# Book material is intentionally excluded from this repo (see CLAUDE.md).
# Several chapter notebooks still write figures/exports into a sibling `book/`
# tree when executed (e.g. beyond-ship-and-pray/book/figures/*.png), which would
# silently re-introduce manuscript artifacts. Ignore those trees outright.
book/
beyond-*/book/
